{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/r1-safety_bypass.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":609091,\"duration_api_ms\":610351,\"num_turns\":20,\"result\":\"Now I have all the information needed to complete the safety_bypass review. Let me analyze the key attack surfaces systematically before producing the output.\\n\\nKey findings from analysis:\\n1. `enable-required-check.sh:301-314` — `--expected-wrapper-sha` compares wrapper pin vs operator-provided SHA, but does NOT verify that SHA is a release-tag SHA. Gate 2 integrity anchor (D-030 `v*` tag-protection) can be bypassed with a non-tag commit.\\n2. `enable-required-check.sh:336-344` — Gate 3 prior-entry detection searches the on-disk log file (`grep -Fq`). If Gate 1's log entry is never committed, Gate 3 sees no prior entry and skips Gate 2 SHA verification requirement.\\n3. `DISPATCH-NOTE.md:9` — `` `cascade-status:` not applicable `` (backtick-formatted) produces 0 regex matches, failing CI on the introducing slice's own PR (also flagged by correctness lens as MAJ-CORR-002, included here for bypass-pressure completeness).\\n4. `enable-required-check.sh:387` — `--restore` JSON shape-validated but source unverified; degraded-state ACK guards partially mitigate.\\n5. `check-invocation-log-entry.sh:169-172` — `branch_log_modified` detected via diff, correctly. But covert invocation without log-entry commit is undetectable.\\n6. Bootstrap-only guard (line 48-50) fires unconditionally before SHA validation (line 154) — guard ordering verified correct.\\n7. Cascade-status fail-closed, regex enforcement, fork-PR refusal, permission ceiling, credential surface — all verified correct.\\n\\n{\\\"lens\\\":\\\"safety_bypass\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Under the SAFETY_BYPASS lens, zero CRIT findings were found — no silent bypass ships waiver content or escalates privileges with a clean audit trace. Two MAJ findings target the break-glass 3-gate procedure. First, enable-required-check.sh --expected-wrapper-sha in Gate 3 only verifies that the adopter wrapper's current pin matches the operator-supplied SHA; it does not verify the SHA is a release-tag SHA. An operator who pinned to an arbitrary main-branch commit in Gate 2 can pass that same SHA to Gate 3, bypassing the release-tag integrity anchor (D-030 v* tag-protection ruleset). Second, Gate 3's prior-entry detection searches the on-disk branch-protection-log.md; if Gate 1's restore log entry is never committed, Gate 3 sees no prior entry and does not require --expected-wrapper-sha or --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification, allowing Gate 3 re-arm without Gate 2 verification. A third MAJ finding (also identified by the correctness lens as MAJ-CORR-002) is included: the 024B DISPATCH-NOTE's backtick-wrapped cascade-status line produces 0 regex matches, causing CI failure on the introducing slice's own PR and creating compliance pressure to merge without CI green. Positive verifications: cascade-status fail-closed fires on all unrecognised values including typos; the bootstrap-only guard (lines 48-50) fires before any SHA validation (line 154) so CI=true cannot trigger the exit-2 path; --restore and --no-enforce-admins are mutually exclusive via the post-parse guard; the adopter wrapper template carries contents:read + statuses:write only with no id-token: or attestations: at workflow level; the scaffolder makes no gh calls, exposing no credential surface; fork-PR refusal if: clause is present and tested. Two MIN findings and one nit cover restore-JSON source trust, covert invocation under blocked-on-adopter-conflict, and the acknowledged 20-char syntactic floor.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MAJ-SAFE-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Gate 3 re-arm --expected-wrapper-sha accepts any 40-char hex SHA, not only release-tag SHAs, bypassing the integrity anchor of Gate 2.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh:301-314: the wrapper_pin extracted from the adopter repo is compared against $EXPECTED_WRAPPER_SHA supplied by the operator. No call is made to the GitHub tags API to verify the SHA corresponds to a tagged release. ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 2 says 'Use this exact SHA as the pin, NOT a main-branch commit SHA' but the script enforces only pin==expected-sha, not expected-sha∈release-tags.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator performing Gate 2 who pins to an arbitrary main-branch commit (not a release tag) then passes that SHA to Gate 3 via --expected-wrapper-sha proceeds with Gate 3 as if the release-tag integrity anchor was satisfied. The only safeguard is human review of the log entry and the tag-protection ruleset on the SCP repo, neither of which is checked by the script.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"In Gate 3 forward-mode, when --expected-wrapper-sha is provided, add a check: gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/refs/tags --jq '[.[].object.sha] | contains([\\\\\\\"$EXPECTED_WRAPPER_SHA\\\\\\\"])'; exit 2 if false. This keeps the gate-2 release-tag requirement machine-enforced rather than advisory-only.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MAJ-SAFE-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Gate 3 forward-mode prior-entry detection checks the on-disk log file, so if Gate 1's restore log entry is uncommitted, Gate 3 skips the Gate 2 SHA verification requirement.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh:336-344: the guard grep -Fq -- \\\\\\\"— ${REPO}@${BRANCH}\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG\\\\\\\" searches the file on disk. If the operator ran --restore (Gate 1) but discarded the emitted log block without committing it, the file contains no prior entry for that repo@branch. The if-block at line 339 does not execute; Gate 3 proceeds without requiring --expected-wrapper-sha or --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"The 3-gate break-glass sequence can collapse to 2 observable gates: Gate 1 (restore, unlogged) followed immediately by Gate 3 (re-arm, no Gate 2 SHA check). Branch protection is restored then re-armed against whatever SHA the wrapper currently pins, bypassing Gate 2's intent of pinning to a known-good release tag.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Replace or augment the on-disk file grep with a git log search: git log --all --grep=\\\\\\\"— ${REPO}@${BRANCH}\\\\\\\" docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md. Alternatively, in Gate 3 forward-mode always require --expected-wrapper-sha or --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification unconditionally (removing the conditional prior-entry check), which aligns with the stated intent that Gate 2 is always required before Gate 3.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MAJ-SAFE-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"024B DISPATCH-NOTE backtick-wraps cascade-status causing 0 regex matches and CI failure on the introducing slice's own PR, creating pressure to merge without CI green.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE.md line 9: '`cascade-status:` not applicable — ...' (backtick code-inline). The python3 re.findall(r'^cascade-status:\\\\\\\\s+([a-z-]+)\\\\\\\\s*$', text, re.M) does not match a line starting with a backtick; returns []. check-invocation-log-entry.sh:127-134 then exits 1 (FAIL-CLOSED). The CI workflow check-invocation-log-entry.yml has no exemption for the 024B DISPATCH-NOTE, which is in the diff path docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md. Test case15b confirms this exact pattern (cascade-status: not applicable with space) yields 0 matches and exit 1. Also identified by correctness lens as MAJ-CORR-002.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"The 024B PR cannot satisfy its own CI-green acceptance criterion. Resolving this without a code fix requires a manual override (disable the required check or force-merge), leaving no audit record and establishing a precedent for bypassing CI on safety-enforcement scripts.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Change the 024B DISPATCH-NOTE to use a bare field such as 'cascade-status: not-applicable' (hyphenated) AND add 'not-applicable' as a recognised exit-0 value in check-invocation-log-entry.sh. Alternatively add an awk carve-out in the CI workflow that skips enforcement when the DISPATCH-NOTE path is docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md specifically.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MIN-SAFE-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"--restore pre-state JSON is shape-validated but not cryptographically bound to a prior invocation log entry; a crafted degraded-state JSON can be supplied by any operator with local access.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"enable-required-check.sh:387 emits 'pre-state JSON should come from a prior invocation log entry' as a warning only. Lines 394-473: the python3 validation checks required keys and types but cannot verify the file originated from a prior run. Degraded states (enforce_admins:false, empty contexts) require ACK flags (--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement, --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks) which partially mitigate accidental use but not deliberate supply of a crafted file.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"An operator with local script access who combines a crafted JSON (enforce_admins:false, empty contexts) with both ACK flags can restore branch protection to a degraded state that removes the SCP required-check gate without any prior legitimate invocation log. The ACK flags are the only barrier; no HMAC or hash comparison against a log-entry checksum is performed.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Compute and record a SHA256 of the pre-state JSON blob at forward-mode invocation time in the log entry. In --restore mode, print the expected checksum from the log entry alongside the 'should come from prior log entry' warning so the operator can verify. Optionally add a --pre-state-checksum flag that the script validates before proceeding.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MIN-SAFE-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Under cascade-status: blocked-on-adopter-conflict, a covert enable-required-check.sh invocation without a committed log entry is undetectable by the CI negative assertion.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"check-invocation-log-entry.sh:169-172: branch_log_modified is set to 1 only when $BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG appears in changed_files (the PR diff). If the operator runs enable-required-check.sh against the target (mutating branch protection) but discards the emitted log block without committing it, the log file does not appear in the diff; branch_log_modified stays 0; the blocked-on-adopter-conflict negative assertion passes. Branch protection is silently mutated while CI shows green.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A slice can declare blocked-on-adopter-conflict (no onboarding claimed), covertly arm the required check by running the script without logging, and pass CI. The mutation is detectable only via out-of-band GitHub audit log. Requires deliberately adversarial operator behaviour; T-024-02 acknowledges the compromised-credential surface but not the covert-no-log-entry variant.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add an additional CI step that queries the GitHub branch-protection API for the target repo (extracted from DISPATCH-NOTE) and asserts the SCP required-check is NOT enabled when cascade-status is blocked-on-adopter-conflict. This converts the negative assertion from a diff-only check to a live API check.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nit-SAFE-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"All-punctuation 20-char TF descriptions pass the regex by design — syntactic floor acknowledged but no automated semantic floor exists.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE worked-example matrix note: '20-char punctuation-only example passes by design'; test case4g: TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-pim (open): -------------------- (20 dashes) → exit 0. The regex \\\\\\\\S.{19,} requires only non-whitespace start + ≥20 chars total; semantic content is a human-review-only control.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A bare stub like '--- conflict filed ---' (21 chars, all punctuation) passes CI and satisfies the format spec while conveying no actionable tracking information. The human review layer is the sole semantic gate.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a minimum-word-count heuristic (e.g., require at least two whitespace-separated tokens: \\\\\\\\S+\\\\\\\\s+\\\\\\\\S+) or a minimum non-punctuation character count. Alternatively document explicitly in ADOPT-001 §12.8 that the regex is a syntactic floor and reviewers must reject description-only-punctuation TF rows.\\\"}]}\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"7a445e28-4b93-424b-b517-2144a3271d68\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.10162685,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":115281,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":594977,\"output_tokens\":32553,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":115281,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":9381,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":98768,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":23894,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":23894},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2367,\"outputTokens\":27,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0025020000000000003,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":32553,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":594977,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":115281,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.09912485,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"d24a414a-f5d3-4b96-90fa-5f179d6720f4\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
