{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"D-044|WP-SCP-024B|024B|scaffold-downstream|check-invocation-log-entry|restore\" docs/DECISIONS.md STATUS.md'","aggregated_output":"docs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-09 (D-044 filed at WP-SCP-024 024B; D-045 / D-046 remain reserved; estate cascade)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 is reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:33:> --restore` rollback mode + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:44:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:91:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B operational contracts for cascade scaffolding (this PR). Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (= `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically — bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments `--adopter-repo`, `--default-branch`, `--scp-sha`, `--scorecard-emit`, `--output-dir` per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12; cascade-onboarded adopters standardise on `policy-check-wrapper.yml`, while pre-cascade manual adopters may still have `policy-check.yml` until they rename to the canonical filename (the §12.7.1 callout covers this carve-out and the follow-on `--wrapper-path` work item). (3) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` mode reverses prior branch-protection mutation from a captured before-state, validates the captured GET-shape JSON, transforms it into the PUT payload by stripping `_links` / `url` / `checks` envelope fields, flattening `enforce_admins.enabled` back to a boolean, preserving `required_pull_request_reviews` recursively, and normalising invalid or absent `restrictions` to null. Restore mode now warns and requires explicit acknowledgements when the captured pre-state would remove `enforce_admins` or clear `required_status_checks.contexts`, captures the observed current branch-protection state immediately before PUT, and mirrors forward-mode's APPLY_FAIL pattern so failed PUTs still emit an audit log before exiting non-zero. New safety check (forward mode only): resolves the canonical wrapper by repo-relative path (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) instead of workflow display name, then refuses to invoke unless the repo has at least one successful `policy-check` workflow run in the last 60 days on the target branch; once a target already has an invocation log entry, forward-mode re-arming requires `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-gate-2>` or the explicit `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` override. (4) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI enforces invariant 2's 4 cascade-status check behaviours: fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; `onboarded` requires log entry + target match; `onboarded-operator-bump` additionally requires STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` requires DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex literally + log file NOT modified. Slug matching canonicalises adopter names to lowercased hyphen-only owner/repo strings so dots/underscores collapse to hyphens before regex matching. Regex (Python re): `TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open|pending|in-progress|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` — matches in STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE; `\\S` anchor at description start prevents all-whitespace bypass; ≥20 chars total. (5) ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure — 3-gate playbook (disable via `--restore` → SHA-pin to last known-good release tag → re-enable after Renovate-bumped fix). The break-glass procedure now documents the `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch as an emergency-only bypass, and the emitted invocation log records a CAUTION line so use of that bypass stays auditable. The new `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` workflow wires `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` into `pull_request` CI and is required-status-check eligible for adopters. All four script components (scaffolder + `--restore` + `--i-understand` flag + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C. Slice 024B itself ships under documented protocol deviation (direct codex exec / claude -p; non-kernel-dangerous shell + tests + docs scope) per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md` note + justify rule; 024C entry is conditional on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure (per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04) per the §9 reservation block; this slice ratifies it. The four-component scope (scaffolder + template + `--restore` + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh`) is the single hardest predecessor surface for cohort cascade — without all four, cascade slices 024C-F would each rebuild the per-adopter wrapper shape, the rollback procedure, and the cascade-status invariant enforcement from scratch (multiplying the 9-round adversarial-review burden that 024A absorbed by 4 cohort slices). The `MANIFEST.json` + SHA256 audit surface mirrors the `install_acc_hook.sh` pattern (atomic config + binary SHA pinning) — provides forensic traceability for cascade-driven adopter-side artefact authorship. The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag closes the cold-start chicken-and-egg: a new adopter has no green CI before the wrapper merges + at least one PR runs, so the safety check would otherwise block first-onboard; the explicit flag is the operator's acknowledgement that they accept the cold-start risk for that single first-onboard run. The break-glass 3-gate procedure is intentionally NOT a one-button kill-switch (all gates auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures adopters don't stay un-gated forever). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation. |\nSTATUS.md:3:**Last updated:** 2026-05-09 (WP-SCP-024 024B - scaffolder + --restore + invocation-log CI; D-044 filed; previous: 2026-05-09 D-035-rules retired)\nSTATUS.md:119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:123:**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\nSTATUS.md:137:**Slice 024B remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope unchanged: scaffolder + `--restore` mode + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + D-044 + real-repo rollback round-trip.\nSTATUS.md:139:## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — slice 024B + protocol-deviation-noted)\nSTATUS.md:143:| 1 | #pending | **024B** | D-044 filed; protocol deviation noted (direct codex exec for 024B; cohort cascade 024C-F gated on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure); plan-doc §6 amended with cohort dispatcher precondition; ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure shipped; scaffolder + template + `--restore` + invocation-log CI + tests all live; `--restore` real-repo round-trip evidence PENDING — operator-interactive demo at step 7 of dispatch plan; evidence path `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` to be committed post-demo, pre-merge, per plan-doc §6 acceptance criterion. |\nSTATUS.md:252:## Tracked-forward items from 024B\nSTATUS.md:255:- **TF-024B-003** (open): forward-mode `enable-required-check.sh` safety check hardcodes `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`; manual adopters using the older `policy-check.yml` naming need a `--wrapper-path` follow-on (tracked here as non-blocking for cascade adopters, which use the canonical wrapper filename).\nSTATUS.md:256:- **TF-024B-002** (open): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence (docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md) — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7; merge-blocking AC per plan-doc §6 + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003; closes when operator runs forward-mode + --restore round-trip on throw-away test repo + commits byte-for-byte match evidence.\nSTATUS.md:257:- **TF-024B-001** (closed): pre-existing shellcheck SC2221+SC2222 warnings on enable-required-check.sh:235 (commit 373bcd29 / slice 020G 2026-04-30) — implicitly closed by fix-round-1's --restore extension rewriting the case-pattern region; shellcheck on enable-required-check.sh now exits 0.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' docs/DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Standards Control Plane — Decision Log\n\n**Last Updated:** 2026-05-09 (D-044 filed at WP-SCP-024 024B; D-045 / D-046 remain reserved; estate cascade)\n\n> **D-021 reservation note (2026-04-28):** D-021 is reserved for the\n> 2026-05-31 atomic workday filing per WP-SCP-019 hygiene response (PR\n> #30, 2026-04-21). Codex executors running WP-SCP-022 implementation\n> slices must NOT assign D-021 to any decision filed during the\n> autonomous run. The WP-SCP-022 §4.7 gate-enforcement helper\n> (`scripts/wp_scp_022_gate_check.sh --check-d021`) detects collisions.\n\n> **D-041 / D-042 / D-043 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 023A):**\n> D-041 is reserved for WP-SCP-023 slice 023B (cross-repo scorecard data\n> shape + opt-in adopter participation model). D-042 is reserved for\n> slice 023C (aggregator pipeline trust model — GitHub Actions Artifact\n> Attestation for adopter emits + SCP-side Ed25519 key registry).\n> **Mandatory trust constraint on D-042 (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001,\n> per WP-SCP-023 §5 step 3):** the 023C aggregator MUST verify the\n> `job_workflow_ref` OIDC claim in each artifact attestation against the\n> SCP reusable workflow path AND SHA pin via `gh attestation verify\n> --signer-workflow <owner>/<repo>/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<sha>`;\n> OIDC JWKS signature verification alone is not sufficient.\n> D-043 is reserved for slice 023D (MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard`\n> shape + read-only contract). Codex executors dispatched for any\n> WP-SCP-023 implementation slice must NOT assign D-041, D-042, or D-043\n> to any other decision filed during that slice. The reservation pattern\n> mirrors the D-021 guard above.\n\n> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\n> D-044 is reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\n> = `SCP-073-scaffolder` operational contract + adopter-template versioning\n> + invocation-log convention extension + `enable-required-check.sh\n> --restore` rollback mode + `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`\n> CI wiring). D-045 is reserved for slice 024C (estate\n> cascade ordering canary-first per WP-SCP-024 §5.1, per-adopter\n> onboarding contract per §5.2, post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar\n> week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle per invariant 8, cascade-slice rollback\n> procedure per invariant 7). D-046 is reserved for slice 024G\n> (estate-cascade Threshold A criteria + post-Threshold-A maintenance\n> posture: recurring drift remediation, version-ramp coordination,\n> departing-adopter procedure; decision on whether `scp.consult_estate_status`\n> ships standalone or rolls into existing `consult_scorecard`). Codex\n> executors dispatched for any WP-SCP-024 implementation slice must NOT\n> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\n> slice. The reservation pattern mirrors the D-021 / D-041–043 guards\n> above.\n\n| ID | Date | Decision | Status | Rationale |\n|----|------|----------|--------|-----------|\n| D-001 | 2026-04-11 | Use Python for the phase 1 CLI-first implementation | ACCEPTED | Fast path to explicit schemas, local tooling, JSON validation, and deterministic file-based execution |\n| D-002 | 2026-04-11 | Keep the project as a standalone app rather than extending docs-agent or Control Tower directly | ACCEPTED | Keeps evaluator runtime independent while still allowing later integration with both systems |\n| D-003 | 2026-04-11 | Limit the first governed implementation slice to standards registry loading, minimal findings loading, and consult retrieval | ACCEPTED | Keeps the first end-to-end work package narrow enough to review rigorously while still allowing real consult output |\n| D-004 | 2026-04-11 | Introduce an explicit project-area intermediate representation before evaluator implementation | ACCEPTED | Keeps evaluator inputs deterministic, testable, and independent from raw repo sprawl |\n| D-005 | 2026-04-11 | Wire governance evaluation through the audit CLI before attempting architecture evaluation | ACCEPTED | Establishes one real evaluator path end to end before widening the audit surface |\n| D-006 | 2026-04-11 | Extend audit and project-area contracts before WP-SCP-003 implementation | ACCEPTED | Governance review evidence and unsupported-domain coverage must be first-class structured data, not implied by prose or raw path scanning |\n| D-007 | 2026-04-11 | Use an explicit unattended-delivery protocol for the remaining programme | ACCEPTED | The remaining work should continue without waiting for user answers, using documented default decisions, bounded review loops, and backlog carry-forward for non-blocking residuals |\n| D-008 | 2026-04-12 | Use explicit file-content signal heuristics for phase-1 architecture evaluation | ACCEPTED | The architecture slice needs deterministic, test-backed checks against repo-local evidence rather than broad semantic inference or prompt-only judgement |\n| D-009 | 2026-04-12 | Add a second repo-backed fixture corpus for architecture signal coverage | ACCEPTED | `ARCH-003` and `ARCH-004` need concrete repo-backed sample files instead of synthetic payload-only tests if the slice is going to prove its own honesty |\n| D-010 | 2026-04-12 | Reconcile findings by deterministic finding ID and area-scoped audit coverage | ACCEPTED | Findings persistence must refresh and resolve records only inside the audited area and evaluated domains so unrelated history is not disturbed |\n| D-011 | 2026-04-12 | Guard findings persistence with scope-collision checks and per-file atomic replacement plus rollback | ACCEPTED | Persisted lifecycle state must fail on `finding_id` scope collisions and should avoid half-written files without pretending phase 1 has a crash-safe multi-file transaction |\n| D-012 | 2026-04-12 | Bind generated report and area-summary timestamps to the current audit timestamp | ACCEPTED | Report outputs need byte-stable reruns and freshness checks, so they should reuse `audit_result.generated_at` rather than inventing wall-clock timestamps |\n| D-013 | 2026-04-12 | Reuse the current write-flow guarantees for report artifacts and carry true bundled transactions to backlog | ACCEPTED | The reporting slice should stay downstream of the existing persistence guarantees instead of pretending to offer a crash-safe cross-artifact commit in phase 1 |\n| D-014 | 2026-04-12 | Guard `report` freshness with embedded findings-state signatures as well as audit timestamp | ACCEPTED | A date-bound audit timestamp alone is too weak to detect same-day content drift, so the report needs a stronger freshness check against persisted findings state |\n| D-015 | 2026-04-12 | Apply waivers as an audit-time overlay rather than embedding waiver rules inside evaluators | ACCEPTED | Evaluators should keep emitting deterministic raw findings so the same checks can be reused with or without waivers, while audit assembly owns exception handling |\n| D-016 | 2026-04-12 | Centralise score calculation in a shared module and count only active unwaived findings against score | ACCEPTED | Score semantics must be documented, deterministic, and consistent across evaluators and audit assembly, and waived issues should not drag active score down |\n| D-017 | 2026-04-12 | Use one embedded fenced JSON review-evidence block as the shared contract for governance validation and historical review retrieval | ACCEPTED | One small structured block inside markdown keeps review evidence inspectable in git while avoiding two drifting review-data formats |\n| D-018 | 2026-04-12 | Keep historical review retrieval as explicit consult output rather than hiding it inside generic guidance text | ACCEPTED | Review history should be visible, bounded, and machine-readable so later consumers can use it without reparsing prose |\n| D-019 | 2026-04-18 | SVC-003 is declare-a-contract with a closed four-mode set (`mode.user_oidc`, `mode.service_rs256`, `mode.api_key`, `mode.bearer_legacy`); commit `66ba8a4` codifies `mode.user_oidc` with no rework; WP-SCP-018 `--auth-token` classifies as `mode.bearer_legacy` with deprecation close date 2026-06-30 | ACCEPTED | Estate reality has three live token types plus a cookie session flow; a single fixed mechanism breaks machine callers; a closed mode set prevents drift; codifying the existing CT OIDC layer keeps the in-repo auth story consistent without forcing a rework |\n| D-020 | 2026-04-18 | `_normalise_scope` accepts `request.scope.area_id` as the normaliser hint when `_infer_area_id` raises `AreaIdInferenceError`; mismatched-inference still raises the same way as before | ACCEPTED | Adopters auditing scopes that lack an ENH-style marker (e.g. a root-level `services.yml` dogfood) would otherwise have to plant placeholder enhancement docs to satisfy area-id inference; the narrow relaxation preserves the auditor discipline of catching inferred-vs-claimed mismatches while closing the genuine uninferrable-scope ergonomic gap |\n| D-022 | 2026-04-21 | Adopt reusable GitHub Actions workflow + OPA/Conftest + Renovate shared preset + required status check with `enforce_admins=true` as the estate's policy federation primitive. Alternatives rejected: `palantir/policy-bot` (GitHub App per org, HCL-not-Rego, no Renovate cascade, no native waiver-overlay); custom control-plane service (build cost, duplicates GH Actions + branch protection primitives) | ACCEPTED | Industry-standard shape; no custom control-plane service required; cheapest path converting SCP from advisory auditor to pre-merge gate; Renovate preset cascade gives \"change one rule → enforce across 10 repos in 24h\"; supports waiver-aware evaluation and structured annotation payloads. Full rationale body in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §10 |\n| D-023 | 2026-04-21 | Reject multi-agent free-form chat-forum pattern as the agent-coordination venue; adopt structured proposal queue (`docs/reviews/proposals/PROP-NNN.md` + MCP `propose()` tool — initial stub in WP-SCP-021 slice 021E; full adjudication workflow in `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue`, separately tracked per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §12). Agents never free-form chat with each other; they read SCP's decision records and call SCP's MCP tools | ACCEPTED | Du et al. (ICML 2024, `arxiv 2305.14325`) show multi-agent debate converges to consensus fast including when the consensus is wrong; Anthropic's multi-agent research post reports ~15× token cost with compounding coordination errors; human-on-the-loop literature converges on moderator-as-bottleneck past a few decisions/hour. Proposal-queue pattern scales because the human is on the loop, not in it. Full rationale body in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §10 (decision originator) and `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 (`propose()` stub design). Note 2026-04-28: original D-023 forward-referenced \"WP-SCP-022 plan when that WP opens\"; WP-SCP-022 v0.2 is the implementation programme plan, not the proposal-queue WP — the rationale-body expansion lives in the parent plans named here, and the adjudication WP is renamed `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue` |\n| D-024 | 2026-04-21 | Adopt Anthropic's Model Context Protocol (MCP) as the estate's agent-to-SCP tool protocol. Transports: stdio (primary, local, trust-the-process) + streamable HTTP (opt-in, bearer-token via `SCP_MCP_TOKEN` with 30-day rotation overlap). Ed25519 asymmetric signing for consult receipts — SCP holds private key; adopters verify with public key published at `scp://security/signing-keys` + committed `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` (90-day rotation overlap). Python `mcp` SDK pinned by version + sdist SHA256; distributed via PyPI as `standards-control-plane[mcp]` extra. OAuth deferred to SCP-075-oauth | ACCEPTED | MCP is the dominant vertical agent-to-tool protocol post Linux Foundation Agentic AI Foundation launch (Dec 2025); Anthropic is protocol origin; Claude Code/Desktop + ACC speak MCP natively. Asymmetric signing prevents adopter-held-key forgery (HMAC symmetric rejected in adversarial review round 1). Alternatives rejected: raw REST (no client ecosystem); custom JSON-RPC (reinvents MCP); gRPC (no agent client support); HMAC symmetric (forgeable by any key-holding adopter). Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 |\n| D-025 | 2026-04-21 | Scoped pre-code consult requirement with Ed25519-signed receipts. Downstream `CLAUDE.md` mandates `scp.consult_rules` before code authoring in governed domains; Claude Code `PreCommit` hook refuses commit without valid receipt. Scope rule: hook consults `scp://rules/domain-map` via `resolve_domain(changed_files)`; non-empty result → receipt required; default-skip globs for docs-only changes. Receipt envelope binds `{schema_version, key_id, repo, head_sha, base_sha, changed_files_hash, domains_covered, issued_at, expires_at ≤ 2h}`; hook validates every field. Break-glass `SCP_MCP_ALLOW_OFFLINE=true` requires committed `docs/overrides/OVERRIDE-NNN.md` with schema-validated expiry ≤ 14d; emits tracked finding SCP-MCP-E010 | ACCEPTED | Client-side enforcement pairs with server-side gate (WP-SCP-020) as belt + braces; scoped + TTL + PR-bound receipts prevent replay/forgery/scope-bypass. Break-glass requires sibling OVERRIDE artefact so fail-closed posture is maintained. Rego gate is authoritative — MCP consult never bypasses. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 |\n| D-026 | 2026-04-28 | Autonomous-dispatch protocol for SCP implementation slices. Each WP-SCP-020 and WP-SCP-021 implementation slice flows through four-tier dispatch: Opus orchestrator (current agent) prepares dispatch package conforming to `~/Projects/acc/schemas/codex_work_package.schema.json`; Codex executor tier runs the slice via `codex_dispatch.py`; 3× parallel Sonnet R1 reviewers apply correctness / safety_bypass / completeness_governance lenses via `claude_dispatch.py` with 500 ms stagger; Opus consolidates verdicts and orchestrates fix rounds. Recurse to fixpoint per `feedback_recursive_adversarial_review.md`. Fix-round budget 5; on budget exhaustion, slice escalates to user review. Evidence persists at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/<slice-id>/`. No slice merges without 3× APPROVED verdict | ACCEPTED | Estate four-tier dispatch standard since 2026-04-22 (per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md`); applies to non-trivial work. SCP implementation slices are non-trivial — they touch CI, branch protection, signing keys, and PyPI. Adversarial review pattern proven on WP-SCP-019 (5 rounds), WP-SCP-020 (5 rounds), WP-SCP-021 (3 rounds, fixpoint). Persisting evidence in-repo gives a permanent audit trail and lets future agents recover from session-bounded amnesia. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4 |\n| D-027 | 2026-04-28 | Parallel-track execution for WP-SCP-020 (federation primitive) and WP-SCP-021 (MCP server) implementation, Scope Y per user 2026-04-28 selection. Both tracks run concurrently from dispatch-zero to user-gate. Track 1 (020): 020B → 020B.1 → 020B.2 → 020C → 020C.1 → 020J → 020K → 020D1 → 020H part 1 → 020E.a → [USER-GATE-A0 release sign-off] → 020H part 2 → 020D2 → [USER-GATE-A] (12 implementation slices + 1 mid-chain human-input gate + 1 terminal gate, matching WP-SCP-020 §3 canonical sequence verbatim). Track 2 (021): 021B → 021C → 021D → 021E → [USER-GATE-C] (4 implementation slices + 1 terminal gate). Concurrent-dispatch limit: 4 active Codex sessions across both tracks. `pyproject.toml` partition: Track 1 owns `[tool.scp.federation]` and adds `scp-policy-check` to `[project.scripts]`; Track 2 owns `[project.optional-dependencies.mcp]` and adds `scp-mcp-server` to `[project.scripts]`. `docs/STATUS.md` excluded from all slice scope_bound