erational contracts for cascade scaffolding (this PR). Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (= `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically — bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments `--adopter-repo`, `--default-branch`, `--scp-sha`, `--scorecard-emit`, `--output-dir` per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12; cascade-onboarded adopters standardise on `policy-check-wrapper.yml`, while pre-cascade manual adopters may still have `policy-check.yml` until they rename to the canonical filename (the §12.7.1 callout covers this carve-out and the follow-on `--wrapper-path` work item). (3) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` mode reverses prior branch-protection mutation from a captured before-state, validates the captured GET-shape JSON, transforms it into the PUT payload by stripping `_links` / `url` / `checks` envelope fields, flattening `enforce_admins.enabled` back to a boolean, preserving `required_pull_request_reviews` recursively, and normalising invalid or absent `restrictions` to null. Restore mode now warns and requires explicit acknowledgements when the captured pre-state would remove `enforce_admins` or clear `required_status_checks.contexts`, captures the observed current branch-protection state immediately before PUT, and mirrors forward-mode's APPLY_FAIL pattern so failed PUTs still emit an audit log before exiting non-zero. New safety check (forward mode only): resolves the canonical wrapper by repo-relative path (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) instead of workflow display name, then refuses to invoke unless the repo has at least one successful `policy-check` workflow run in the last 60 days on the target branch; once a target already has an invocation log entry, forward-mode re-arming requires `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-gate-2>` or the explicit `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` override. Fix-round-7 adds two more guardrails: the `check-invocation-log-entry.yml` workflow path-filters out 024A/024B tooling slices; `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` exits 0 on `cascade-status: not applicable` for tooling slices; `--expected-wrapper-sha` must be a release-tag SHA (queried via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/tags --paginate --jq '.[].commit.sha'`); and Gate 3 now checks both committed log entries and uncommitted `git diff HEAD docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` state before re-arming. (4) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI enforces invariant 2's 4 cascade-status check behaviours: fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; `onboarded` requires log entry + target match; `onboarded-operator-bump` additionally requires STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` requires DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex literally + log file NOT modified. Slug matching canonicalises adopter names to lowercased hyphen-only owner/repo strings so dots/underscores collapse to hyphens before regex matching. Regex (Python re): `TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open|pending|in-progress|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` — matches in STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE; `\\S` anchor at description start prevents all-whitespace bypass; ≥20 chars total. (5) ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure — 3-gate playbook (disable via `--restore` → SHA-pin to last known-good release tag → re-enable after Renovate-bumped fix). The break-glass procedure now documents the `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch as an emergency-only bypass, and the emitted invocation log records a CAUTION line so use of that bypass stays auditable. The new `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` workflow wires `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` into `pull_request` CI and is required-status-check eligible for adopters. All four script components (scaffolder + `--restore` + `--i-understand` flag + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C. Slice 024B itself ships under documented protocol deviation (direct codex exec / claude -p; non-kernel-dangerous shell + tests + docs scope) per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md` note + justify rule; 024C entry is conditional on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure (per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04) per the §9 reservation block; this slice ratifies it. The four-component scope (scaffolder + template + `--restore` + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh`) is the single hardest predecessor surface for cohort cascade — without all four, cascade slices 024C-F would each rebuild the per-adopter wrapper shape, the rollback procedure, and the cascade-status invariant enforcement from scratch (multiplying the 9-round adversarial-review burden that 024A absorbed by 4 cohort slices). The `MANIFEST.json` + SHA256 audit surface mirrors the `install_acc_hook.sh` pattern (atomic config + binary SHA pinning) — provides forensic traceability for cascade-driven adopter-side artefact authorship. The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag closes the cold-start chicken-and-egg: a new adopter has no green CI before the wrapper merges + at least one PR runs, so the safety check would otherwise block first-onboard; the explicit flag is the operator's acknowledgement that they accept the cold-start risk for that single first-onboard run. The break-glass 3-gate procedure is intentionally NOT a one-button kill-switch (all gates auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures adopters don't stay un-gated forever). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation. |\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:133:if [ \"$dispatch_note_mode\" = \"not applicable\" ]; then\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:134:  printf 'OK: DISPATCH-NOTE declares cascade-status: not applicable; not a cohort cascade slice — nothing to enforce\\n'\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:157:  \"not applicable\")\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:158:    printf 'OK: DISPATCH-NOTE declares cascade-status: not applicable; not a cohort cascade slice — nothing to enforce\\n'\nscripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:162:    die \"FAIL-CLOSED: cascade-status field absent or unrecognised; must be one of {onboarded, onboarded-operator-bump, blocked-on-adopter-conflict, not applicable}\"\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:9:cascade-status: not applicable — this slice does not onboard a cohort adopter; it ships the scaffolder + helpers that 024C–F will consume. CI gate `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (which this slice introduces) does not apply to this slice's own PR.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
